  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2786ad2d-c904-4b11-98f3-fed3dd0327b6",
      "name": "How It Works, Setup & Customization",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1888,
        752
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 692,
        "height": 668,
        "content": "**AI Voice Receptionist: Vapi + Google Calendar + Twilio SMS**\n\n**How it works**\nA Vapi voice assistant calls this workflow's webhook during a call. Each tool call goes to its own branch: Google Calendar for availability and bookings, Twilio for confirmation texts, Google Sheets for callback messages. Missed calls get a follow-up text, and replies to that text get an automatic answer.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Connect Google Calendar, Google Sheets and Twilio credentials.\n2. Replace every YOUR_ placeholder (calendar ID, Twilio number, sheet ID) and [YOUR_CLINIC_NAME] in the SMS texts.\n3. Create these columns in your sheet: Time, Name, Phone, Reason.\n4. In Vapi, add six tools named check_availability, book_appointment, find_booking, reschedule_booking, cancel_booking and take_message, using the Vapi Webhook production URL as Server URL. Send end-of-call-report events to Vapi Events Webhook.\n5. In Twilio, set your number's incoming SMS webhook to SMS Reply Webhook.\n6. Set Workflow Settings > Timezone to your clinic's timezone.\n\n**Customization**\nHours, slot length and closed days are at the top of Build Slots. The default phone country code is at the top of Parse Vapi.\n\n**Good to know**\nThe greeting, FAQs and call flow live in the Vapi assistant prompt, not in n8n. Rescheduling does not check for conflicts, so check availability first. Cancel and reschedule need the event ID from find_booking.\n\n**Before activating**\nThis workflow edits your real calendar and sends real SMS. Test with your own phone first."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
